id=a52sxq_play_system_updates
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Google Play system update diagnostics
author=kusti420
description=Testers report Play system updates "broken again" without a reason, and the evidence is gone by the time anyone looks: a failed update boot is rolled back by apexd/vold (the /data checkpoint is discarded, logs and the updated APEXes with it). Adds /system/bin/k4-mainline-diag (adb shell k4-mainline-diag [-v|-s]): one line with the verdict for the newest staged update batch (pending / applied / failed and why: apexd mtime denial, re-signed APEX, ROM flashed before the reboot, crashing native process, rollback after the boot, ...), plus a Tethering BPF check (does the active or the last staged Tethering's netd.o define maps our frozen a52_netd.o lacks). Adds /system/etc/init/a52sxq_mainline.rc, init builtins only (no new SELinux domain): on an update boot (apexd.packages.updated=true) it copies the staged Tethering netd.o and the APEX version lists to /cache/k4_mainline before the BPF loader runs, and if that boot never reaches boot_completed, the next boot keeps its kernel log (pstore) there too. /cache is not checkpointed, so the evidence survives the rollback. Read-only towards the update machinery: it never aborts, deletes or retries a session.
